Cache Heavy Work Out of update()
​Remember that update() is called dozens of times a second whenever the mouse moves over your window.
​Do not parse XML/JSON, format large strings, sort vectors, or run regex inside update().
​Compute your display state once when the user edits something or loads a file, store the result in your struct, and only let update() read references to that pre-computed state.